        {
          "id": "d-730339a6f12064a3/b10_0001",
          "kind": "caption",
          "text": "Table 3 TEAEs of grade ≥ 3 occurring in at least 2 patients in any treatment group.",
          "bbox": {
            "x0": 42.5196,
            "y0": 58.27306599999997,
            "x1": 320.81132131000004,
            "y1": 65.31297800000004
          },
          "page": 10,
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "font_size": null,
          "bold": null,
          "source": "docling",
          "ocr_engine": null
        },
        {
          "id": "d-730339a6f12064a3/b10_0002",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Abbreviation: TEAE, treatment-emergent adverse event.",
          "bbox": {
            "x0": 42.5196,
            "y0": 298.017066,
            "x1": 218.66525135999998,
            "y1": 304.61697799999996
          },
          "page": 10,
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "font_size": null,
          "bold": null,
          "source": "docling",
          "ocr_engine": null
        },
        {
          "id": "d-730339a6f12064a3/b10_0003",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "inhibition,  a  phenomenon  that  has  been  reported  in  studies  of solid  tumors  and  can  eventually  lead  to  drug  resistance. 27,28 Better understanding of the role PI3K signaling plays in myelofibrosis could inform additional targets within this pathway that could  be  inhibited  simultaneously  to  counteract  an  adaptative response.",
          "bbox": {
            "x0": 42.51959999999997,
            "y0": 321.972,
            "x1": 288.081,
            "y1": 387.9453
          },
          "page": 10,
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "font_size": null,
          "bold": null,
          "source": "docling",
          "ocr_engine": null
        },
        {
          "id": "d-730339a6f12064a3/b10_0004",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "In conclusion, findings from  the interim analysis of the LIMBER-304  study  suggested  adding  parsaclisib  to  stable-dose ruxolitinib was unlikely to provide clinically meaningful benefits in  heavily  pretreated  patients  with  myelofibrosis  and  suboptimal or declining response to ruxolitinib, resulting in study termination. The overall incidence of TEAEs was similar between the 2 treatment groups, but there was a greater incidence of serious, severe,  and  fatal  TEAEs,  as  well  as  infection  and  GI  disorders with  the  parsaclisib/ruxolitinib  combination.  Given  the  overall findings, close monitoring for infections and toxicities and reassessment of benefit-risk for patients on combination therapy is warranted.  Further  investigations  may  clarify  if  PI3K  inhibitors could  have  a  role  in  selected  patient  subsets,  or  in  alternative combinations, as potential therapeutic strategies in myeloproliferative neoplasms.",
          "bbox": {
            "x0": 42.5196,
            "y0": 391.5336,
            "x1": 288.11340000000007,
            "y1": 562.0484999999999
          },
          "page": 10,
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "font_size": null,
          "bold": null,
          "source": "docling",
          "ocr_engine": null
        },
        {
          "id": "d-730339a6f12064a3/b10_0005",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "Acknowledgments",
          "bbox": {
            "x0": 42.5196,
            "y0": 583.457934,
            "x1": 169.23291749999999,
            "y1": 597.0980219999999
          },
          "page": 10,
